   "detail": {
    "seconds": 7.34,
    "decision": "proceed",
    "plan": "Question: Investigate whether footwear return rates are unusually high and which product segments, fit outcomes and reported reasons are associated with returns.\nMetrics: return_rate, delivered_lines = count of sale lines with delivered_at not null, return_requested_lines = count of sale lines with return_requested_at not null\nBreakdowns: category; footwear sub_category and article_type, footwear return_reason; footwear size_fit\nFilters: sales.line_type = 'Sale'; product_master.category = 'Footwear' for footwear-specific analyses\nTime window: 2026-01-01 to 2026-10-24 inclusive, by sales.placed_at\nComparison: Footwear return_rate versus other categories in the same order cohort; compare rates across footwear segments and size_fit values.\nExpected result: Separate aggregated tables: one row per category; one row per footwear sub_category and article_type; one row per footwear size_fit; and one row per return_reason among footwear lines with a return request. Include return_rate, delivered_lines and return_requested_lines where applicable; reason table shows return_requested_lines. Limit each table to 50 rows, prioritizing the highest return-request volumes.\nAssumptions: Use a year-to-date order cohort, excluding the last three weeks to reduce return-maturity bias; some orders may still be in transit or awaiting returns.; Return reasons and size_fit describe associations, not proof of cause; retain missing values as an explicit group."
   },
   "t": 7.46
  },
  {
   "type": "step",
   "step": "write_sql",
   "status": "started",
   "detail": {},
   "t": 7.47
  },
  {
   "type": "step",
   "step": "write_sql",
   "status": "done",
   "detail": {
    "seconds": 14.55,
    "attempt": 1,
    "sql": "WITH cohort AS (\n  SELECT p.category, p.sub_category, p.article_type, s.size_fit, s.return_reason,\n         s.delivered_at, s.return_requested_at\n  FROM sales s\n  LEFT JOIN product_master p ON p.product_id = s.product_id\n  WHERE s.line_type = 'Sale'\n    AND s.placed_at >= TIMESTAMP '2026-01-01'\n    AND s.placed_at < TIMESTAMP '2026-10-25'\n)\nSELECT breakdown, category, sub_category, article_type, size_fit, return_reason,\n       return_rate, delivered_lines, return_requested_lines\nFROM (\n  (SELECT 'category' AS breakdown, COALESCE(s.category, '(missing)') AS category,\n          NULL AS sub_category, NULL AS article_type, NULL AS size_fit, NULL AS return_reason,\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL) / NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL), 0) AS return_rate,\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL) AS delivered_lines,\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL) AS return_requested_lines\n   FROM cohort s\n   GROUP BY COALESCE(s.category, '(missing)')\n   ORDER BY return_requested_lines DESC, category\n   LIMIT 50)\n  UNION ALL\n  (SELECT 'footwear_segment', 'Footwear', COALESCE(s.sub_category, '(missing)'),\n          COALESCE(s.article_type, '(missing)'), NULL, NULL,\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL) / NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL), 0),\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL),\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL) AS return_requested_lines\n   FROM cohort s\n   WHERE s.category = 'Footwear'\n   GROUP BY COALESCE(s.sub_category, '(missing)'), COALESCE(s.article_type, '(missing)')\n   ORDER BY return_requested_lines DESC, 3, 4\n   LIMIT 50)\n  UNION ALL\n  (SELECT 'footwear_size_fit', 'Footwear', NULL, NULL, COALESCE(s.size_fit, '(missing)'), NULL,\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL) / NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL), 0),\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL),\n          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL) AS return_requested_lines\n   FROM cohort s\n   WHERE s.category = 'Footwear'\n   GROUP BY COALESCE(s.size_fit, '(missing)')\n   ORDER BY return_requested_lines DESC, 5\n   LIMIT 50)\n  UNION ALL\n  (SELECT 'footwear_return_reason', 'Footwear', NULL, NULL, NULL, COALESCE(s.return_reason, '(missing)'),\n          NULL, NULL, COUNT(*) AS return_requested_lines\n   FROM cohort s\n   WHERE s.category = 'Footwear' AND s.return_requested_at IS NOT NULL\n   GROUP BY COALESCE(s.return_reason, '(missing)')\n   ORDER BY return_requested_lines DESC, 6\n   LIMIT 50)\n) results\nORDER BY CASE breakdown WHEN 'category' THEN 1 WHEN 'footwear_segment' THEN 2\n                        WHEN 'footwear_size_fit' THEN 3 ELSE 4 END,\n         return_requested_lines DESC, category, sub_category, article_type, size_fit, return_reason",
    "explanation": "Returns four labeled breakdowns in one result, each limited to 50 groups by return-request volume. The order cohort excludes the last three weeks, but some returns may still be immature; fit and reason associations do not establish causation."
   },
